[00:26.94] The rusted chains of prison moons
[00:29.92] Are shattered by the sun.
[00:33.26] I walk a road, horizons change
[00:36.16] The tournaments begun.
[00:40.02] The purple piper plays his tune,
[00:43.46] The choir softly sing
[00:46.62] Three lullabies in an ancient tongue,
[00:50.06] For the court of the crimson king.
[00:54.58] The keeper of the city keys
[00:59.04] Put shutters on the dreams.
[01:24.16] I wait outside the pilgrims door
[01:28.84] With insufficient schemes.
[01:32.58] The black queen chants
[01:34.54] The funeral march,
[01:36.10] The cracked brass bells will ring;
[01:39.78] To summon back the fire witch
[01:42.64] To the court of the crimson king.
[03:11.92] The gardener plants an evergreen
[03:15.86] Whilst trampling on a flower.
[03:19.62] I chase the wind of a prism ship
[03:23.22] To taste the sweet and sour.
[03:26.82] The pattern juggler lifts his hand
[03:30.36] The orchestra begin.
[03:34.24] As slowly turns the grinding wheel
[03:37.02] In the court of the crimson king.
[05:09.40] On soft gray mornings widows cry
[05:12.84] The wise men share a joke.
[05:16.38] I run to grasp divining signs
[05:19.98] To satisfy the hoax.
[05:23.40] The yellow jester does not play
[05:26.90] But gentle pulls the strings
[05:30.58] And smiles as the puppets dance
[05:33.54] In the court of the crimson king.
